  "summary": "Thirteen published single-cell tumor microenvironment studies, mostly on macrophage and myeloid suppressor biology; no item addresses miR-ac4C directly.",
  "synthesis": "The 13 published items cluster on single-cell and tumor microenvironment profiling across solid tumors, with emphasis on myeloid compartments. Recurrent themes include tumor-associated macrophages: TREM2+ macrophages in cholangiocarcinoma and HCC, and macrophage lipid signaling driving glioblastoma invasion. Myeloid-derived suppressor cells appear in HCC via THBS1-SDC4 signaling and in melanoma via MGP-high fibroblasts and TNF signaling. Other studies address STAT3-CCL2 signaling in inflammation-associated colorectal cancer, lactate-driven histone lactylation in colorectal liver metastasis, and AhR blockade enhancing anti-PD-1 response. No item addresses miR-ac4C directly, and no preprint, code, or industry signals were recorded. The observed activity consists of a 2.37 rise ratio in published output only.",
